// Unicode simple case mapping for `upper`/`lower` (BACKLOG section 12 item 1).

// ASCII is unchanged.
assertEq("abc".upper(), "ABC");
assertEq("ABC".lower(), "abc");
assertEq("Hello, World!".upper(), "HELLO, WORLD!");
assertEq("Hello, World!".lower(), "hello, world!");

// Latin-1 letters are mapped, and the mapping does not touch other bytes.
assertEq("á".upper(), "Á");
assertEq("Á".lower(), "á");
assertEq("ÉÀÇÜ".lower(), "éàçü");
assertEq("éàçü".upper(), "ÉÀÇÜ");

// Non-ASCII, non-letter text is copied byte for byte.
assertEq("日本語".upper(), "日本語");
assertEq("日本語".lower(), "日本語");

// Greek: capital to small maps every code point, including the final sigma
// (U+03C2), which is a positional mapping and is mapped to U+03C3 here.
assertEq("ΣΊΣΥΦΟΣ".lower(), "σίσυφοσ");

// A title-case digraph maps like its upper/lower case.
assertEq("ǅ".upper(), "Ǆ");
assertEq("Ǆ".lower(), "ǆ");

// A code point whose full mapping expands to several code points has no simple
// mapping and is left unchanged: `ß` -> "SS", `İ` -> "i" + combining dot, and
// the `ﬁ` ligature -> "FI" are all returned as-is.
assertEq("straße".upper(), "STRAßE");
assertEq("İ".lower(), "İ");
assertEq("ﬁ".upper(), "ﬁ");

// Round-trip: lowering an upper-cased ASCII word returns the original.
assertEq("Oskel".upper().lower(), "oskel");

print("unicode case ok");
